 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Extension by zero preserves the finite-Tor constructible category",
 "statement": "Let $j:U\\hookrightarrow Y$ be an open immersion admitting a compactification,\nlet $a\\le b$ be integers, and let $K$ be a bounded constructible complex of\n$\\Lambda$-modules on $U$ with cohomology concentrated in $[a,b]$ and Tor\namplitude in $[a,b]$. Then $Rj_!K$ is bounded constructible on $Y$, with\ncohomology concentrated in $[a,b]$ and Tor amplitude in $[a,b]$; in particular\n$j_!$ carries $\\Dctf(U,\\Lambda)$ into $\\Dctf(Y,\\Lambda)$ without moving the\ninterval.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-six-functors/sk-lem-sf-open-ctf/_section.md",
  "place": "node sk-lem-sf-open-ctf, order 2499"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "sk-def-sf-operations"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "$j_!$ is exact, so\n$\\mathcal H^r(j_!K)=j_!\\mathcal H^r(K)$ and the range does not grow; a finite\nstratification of $U$ witnessing constructibility, together with the closed\ncomplement $Y\\setminus U$, stratifies $Y$; and the amplitude is tested by\nrestricting an arbitrary sheaf on $Y$ to $U$.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  }
 ],
